      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1407 and 903, we can use the Euclidean algorithm, which is an efficient method for computing the greatest common divisor of two integers. This algorithm is based on the principle that the GCD of two numbers also divides their difference. Here is how I would approach it:\n\n1. Start with the two numbers, 1407 and 903.\n\n2. The Euclidean algorithm works by repeatedly replacing the larger number with its remainder when divided by the smaller number. The process continues until one of the numbers reaches 0.\n\n   a. Since 1407 is larger than 903, we divide 1407 by 903, and take 903 as the new dividend, 1407 as the new divisor, and 0 as the remainder.\n\n   1407 ÷ 903 = 1 remainder 504\n\n2. Now we replace the original values with the remainder we just calculated, 903 with 1407, and 0 with 504.\n\n   The new values are 903, 1407, and 504.\n\n3. Repeat step 2:\n\n   a. Since 1407 is the new larger number, we divide 1407 by 504 and take 504 as the new dividend, 1407 as the new divisor, and 0 as the remainder.\n\n   1407 ÷ 504 = 2 remainder 405\n\n4. Now we replace the original values with the remainder we just calculated, 504 with the remainder 1407, and 0 with 405. So, 504 becomes the new 504. \n\n   The new values are 504, 1407, and 405.\n\n5. Perform step 2 again:\n\n   Since 1407 is still the larger number, we divide 1407 by 405 and take 405 as the new 1407.\n\n   1407 ÷ 405 = 3 remainder 12\n\n6. Continue with step 2:\n\n   405 becomes the new 504, and 1407 becomes the new 405.\n\n   1407 ÷ 405 = 3 remainder 12.\n\n   405 becomes the new 405, and 1407 becomes the new 12.\n\n7. Since 12 is less than 405, our division now yields 12 and 405.\n\n8. Finally, we had a remainder of 405, which we divided by a remainder of 12 resulting in the answer of 3.\n\nSince, after all these divisions, the process stopped, what was considered our last step, we know we will stop here. Therefore, the remainder, which is 12, represents the GCD.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 1407 and 903 is 3,\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
