      "text": "Step 1: Find the prime factorization of 1407 and 903.\nTo find the prime factorization, we divide the largest number by the largest prime factor and continue the process until we reach 1.\nPrime factorization of 1407:\n1407 is not divisible by 2, so we try 3.\n1407 divided by 3 is 469.\n469 is not divisible by 2 or 3, so we try 7.\n469 divided by 7 is 67.\n67 is a prime number, so we stop here.\nPrime factorization of 1407: 3 * 7 * 67.\n\nPrime factorization of 903:\n903 is not divisible by 2, so we try 3.\n903 divided by 3 is 301.\n301 is not divisible by 2, 3, or 5, so we try 7.\n301 divided by 7 is 43.\n43 is a prime number, so we stop here.\nPrime factorization of 903: 3 * 7 * 43.\n\nStep 2: Find the GCD.\nTo find the GCD, we multiply the common prime factors.\nThe common prime factors between 1407 and 903 are 3 and 7.\nThe GCD = 3 * 7 = 21.\n\nThe greatest common divisor of 1407 and 903 is 21.",
